{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/93840-wraith-logistics","id":93840,"title":"Wraith Logistics","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-03-18T15:23:09-07:00","id":93840,"title":"Wraith Logistics","content":"Okay a lot of times it seems the authors of Wraith were not on the same page when talking about quantities and such of various things. For instance we have Soul Forging as the source of Most of the Material in the Underworld, with scavenged relics second, and harvested items originating in the Underworld a far third. But not everyone who dies becomes a Wraith, and not every Wraith that is reaped is made a citizen as many are enslaved or forged off the bat. And then we have Drones, where a lot of ghosts are mindless, these are often harvested and forged when found.<br /> <br /> But we have things like whole towers built from Souls... yet Soulsteel only makes an amount of Soulsteel in the volume of the ghost forged, often I get the impression at a lesser density. Not to mention White Jade makes only 10 pounds per level of corpus. Many seem to forget that items crafted from Soulsteel in general take a whole soul, regardless of how tiny as Soulsteel is very disinclined to be split up. So the logistics of having all these towers fully furbished with chairs and desks all made out of souls seems a bit much sometimes.<br /> <br /> And each Obol is a condensed soul and can be crafted into an object the size of the original soul, but some authors seem to forget this and it becomes clear.<br /> <br /> But with these logistics doesn't seem odd when you get things like a standing bounty of obols for Specter Teeth, I mean Dozen obols should be a friggin lot, thats a dozen souls! It seems a bit much to make each Specter worth so many souls...<br /> <br /> <br /> And specters we really have no indicator how many there are, sometimes you get the feeling that there are more specters generated then Wraiths. But a lot of this can be deceiving because you also get the impression that the turn over rate for Wraiths is much higher then for specters. Like if you know a wraith existed a year ago you have no idea if its still around because it could have been sent to oblivion, transcended, or soul forged, yet with a Specter... the assumption seems to be if you know a specter existed a year ago they are likely still around because the turnover rate of existing in a made storm riding horde for some reason is not that high compared to sane folks.<br /> <br /> And then you get contradictions, in the beginning of the Dark Kingdom of Jade Book they state Kuei can be forged into white jade but it isn't permanent and it often degrades over time, yet later in the book with they talk about the Way of the Farmer and how corpus harvested by Kuei can be used as material, not really clear on if this is normal white jade, and they seem to imply it works just like normal white jade with no issues. They don't even say if you can keep harvesting the Kuei, or if the Corpus you Harvest from them is permanently removed, I guess I'll wager on the conservative side and say its permanent loss.<br /> <br /> But the Angst accumulation gets astronomic for folks like Soul Forgers and Hell Torturers, often the NPCs are not written with the idea that they have to get regularly Pardoned of Angst into their character.<br /> <br /> And how do you explain the Logistics of making the Emperors Palace, its a virtual city hundreds of miles across with over 250 palaces made of white jade, and other buildings besides that... If a single souls can make a building block somewhere between the size of a bucket and a desk... you would still need an insane amount of souls to make even a single palace... not to mention 250 + Multi story palaces. And then they also paved an Imperial Highway!<br /> <br /> And then we also have the Pathos Economy which most of the books seem to forget exists. What with Pathos Money in the Dark Kingdom of Jade being impermanent if created by Wraiths. I think the Stygian version runs off of Pathos Batteries right?<br /> <br /> This really makes it sound like there should be a bigger business of Importing Building Material from the Isles of the Tempest, as well as smuggling items from the Living World into Relic form using magic, or at least emotionally resonant ritualistic destruction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-18T18:38:53-07:00","id":93999,"title":"","content":"I only had a little experience with Wraith and then they discontinued it and i did my own thing with Wraiths being treated a lot more like spirits mechanically then like PCs. What little I got to interact with them worked on the principle that there were inanimate reflections of historically potent events and places. These after images of war camps, castles, and various other forgotten memories were how the kingdoms were able to function logistically. This allows for salvaging operations to be important story lines for characters to take part in, both as workers and guardians, and accounts for forgers having a purpose without having to allows forge squishy souls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-18T21:30:59-07:00","id":94083,"title":"","content":"I would keep in mind many, many people have died in human history. Charon has been around since, or possibly before, classical antiquity, so there has been a lot of time to build up materials. Soulsteel doesn't, as far as I'm aware, degrade, so that is a long time to build materials.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-18T23:17:55-07:00","id":94133,"title":"","content":"As to the question of &quot;raw materials,&quot; I actually addressed this in another thread. It's estimated that 150,000 people die <i>every day</i>, and even if only 10% of them become wraiths, that's still 15,000, and then, if we were to do a very charitable even split, that's 5000 new Drones, 5000 new Spectres, and 5000 regular wraiths, in any given 24-hour period. Drones alone, that's more than the Artificers can process in a day, even if only 10% of the Drones are being Reaped by Stygia - they're also processing criminals and such, as well. And that's a <i><b>day</b></i>. Stygia's been going for hundreds of years. Plus, you have things like the Library of Alexandria - buildings destroyed in the Skinlands that they've moved to the Isle, and other refuse and flotsam.<br /> <br /> Existence is cheap in the Underworld.<br /> <br /> Now, the Pathos economy... Think if that as more like black market, &quot;favor-for-a-favor&quot; kind of thing. It's closer to a drug deal than it is buying something from a store.<br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-19T01:01:22-07:00","id":94159,"title":"","content":"Thousands of people die every day. A small big of those thousands become wraiths. Most of those wraiths are Drones. Even if the Hierarchy was hilariously ineffective, they'd still have mountains of material to work with in a very short amount of time, and that's not factoring in those who go to the forges for their crimes. Now extrapolate that math back hundreds of years; let's just say, the Artificiers won't go jobless any time soon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-19T05:36:53-07:00","id":94213,"title":"","content":"I'd be more worried about the fact that in 1900 there were more people alive than there had been <i>in all of human history combined</i>. So the question isn't really how they do it <i>now</i> so much as how they did it <i>before</i>. I mean sure, now they can do it 'cause life comes cheap - but what'd they do when there were fewer people/to die?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/426-big-brother","name":"Big Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar426_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-19T08:55:47-07:00","id":94278,"title":"","content":"Maybe people cared more about their stuff so more raw material was crossing over? Then you need less of whatever you want to call something that is so much worse than slavery. Plus, all settlements were a lot smaller and their Shadowlands counterparts were probably too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-19T11:41:01-07:00","id":94354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Big Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/93840-wraith-logistics?p=94213#post94213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd be more worried about the fact that in 1900 there were more people alive than there had been <i>in all of human history combined</i>. So the question isn't really how they do it <i>now</i> so much as how they did it <i>before</i>. I mean sure, now they can do it 'cause life comes cheap - but what'd they do when there were fewer people/to die?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I was more concerned about this, since many of what I was talking about were erected before modern day, though I was always skeptical about the declaration of more people then ever died.<br /> <br /> But you all also seem to forget that all the dead don't go to Stygia, Swar and the Dark Kingdom of Jade alone has nearly half of the Worlds dead. So all these numbers being used should be at a fraction of the stated number for any one Dark Kingdom.<br /> <br /> And Swar goes around turning people into grapes... come on one Wraith into 10 grapes... that is a silly way to make feasts.<br /> <br /> So a Thousand years ago they could make hundreds of palaces out of only the Wraiths in Asia? That seems a bit much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-19T11:59:55-07:00","id":94366,"title":"","content":"There aren't more people alive than now than have ever died. That's a myth. <a href=\"http://www.snopes.com/science/stats/dead.asp\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.snopes.com/science/stats/dead.asp</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-19T13:13:29-07:00","id":94407,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\">This logistics debate came up several times in my troupe. We threw around a few ideas. One was \u201cwraith-farming\u201d (as Mr. D would call it many years later), but that notion never sat well with me. Mechanically, it was too similar to Moliate. Thematically, it caused soulsteel to lose some of its forlorn dread (having a sword made out of someone\u2019s Corpus isn\u2019t nearly as foreboding/cool as having a sword made from someone\u2019s SOUL). The biggest thing that confused us was the economic factor of the Obolus; how did you take your averaged sized soul and condense into a coin. [We realized we were dealing with the metaphysical abstractions of ectoplasmic matter, but we still felt like there was a little gap that needed calking.]<br /> <br /> Here\u2019s what my troupe came up with:<br /> <br /> -Forging Soulsteel-<br /> </span><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:courier new\">Ectoplasmic being (Wraith, Spectre, Drone, etc.) is \u201csent to the forge.\u201d </span></li> </ul><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:courier new\">At the forge, it is melted down and cast into a soulsteel ingot (we were thinking about the size of a cinder block). </span></li> </ul><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:courier new\">After the ingot is cast, it can be used to forge other objects. From this single ingot, several items can be hammered out (or material for one large item).</span></li> </ul><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"> <br /> We never did any number crunching, but the idea was you could get a few items from a single ingot, without losing the thematic elements of soulsteel. Off the top of my head, from one ingot, you might be able to forge:<br /> </span><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:courier new\">4-6 swords, depending on size. In our games, the standard-issue Stygian soulsteel sword was a Maintz-style gladius with a stylized bone handle. An ingot could make 6 of these. (I\u2019m guessing maybe 2 or 3 two handed swords or a single Pyramid Head-esque cleaver).</span></li> </ul><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:courier new\">2-3 Breastplates</span></li> </ul><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:courier new\">About 10 Oboli. The whole \u201cworth one soul\u201d becomes more of a metaphor. </span></li> </ul><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"> <br /> We ran a few Doomslaying excursions and it didn\u2019t make sense that, even if the Anacreon was ripping us off, that we\u2019d get two whole souls (two oboli) for one Spectre head. We went this route solely to help with the economic considerations of our suspension of disbelief.<br /> <br /> <b>[Disclaimer: In the \u201cAsk the Deadguy\u201d thread, Mr. D has stated that it\u2019s one soul per object, so this goes directly against the words of THE developer. The above was my troupe\u2019s HR; its presentation is not intended as a challenge to the edicts of the RL Charon. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />]</b></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-19T13:37:25-07:00","id":94432,"title":"","content":"It goes too far against the themes for my taste to have multiple things forged from one soul.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/93840-wraith-logistics?p=94366#post94366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There aren't more people alive than now than have ever died. That's a myth. <a href=\"http://www.snopes.com/science/stats/dead.asp\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.snopes.com/science/stats/dead.asp</a></div> </div> </div> </div>I thought so! It just never made any sense! I mean all of human prehistory and history is a long azz time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-20T00:32:16-07:00","id":94761,"title":"","content":"10 Oboli is a king's ransom in Oboli. I have the first edition with the wealth Background, and the high end for that is seven Oboli, which is the equivalent of a millionaire among the living. The 12 Oboli bounty for spectre teeth mentioned above (I would like a page or book reference at least) is likely either an author fucking up on estimating costs, or it goes to show how incredibly dangerous spectre hunting is, because it means one successful trip could have you set for a century.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-20T00:52:54-07:00","id":94774,"title":"","content":"Page 36 of Doomslayers, the payoff sidebar, its 4 oboli per proven specter killed/restrained specter brought to them. I forgot the number, I just knew it seemed unreasonable. Specters are dangerous but 4 obols is a lot when any items are rare and precious in the underworld. If you are a serious badazz you could make a helluva living by just killing a small handful of specters, much less making a career of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-20T01:57:59-07:00","id":94800,"title":"","content":"Making a career out of it would be a good way to wind up obliviated. The money is good, although the rub is you need to survive, you need to be able to get proof, and the reward likely has to get split among your teammates. So much like any dangerous profession the money is pretty decent if you survive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-20T02:20:58-07:00","id":94808,"title":"","content":"I've often had the same questions mulling around my head.<br /> <br /> I think the best idea I had was that soulsteel is incredibly dense and malleable, as well as incredibly strong. An Obol is very, very heavy for it's size. A soulsteel chair is really an inner frame of ectoplasm or the like, with a soul hammered around it. Ditto swords and so on. You could make a soulsteel skyrise out of one soul if you wished, by the soulsteel needs to be malleated incredibly thinly around the structure to do so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Open the gates of Hell: Random Demon Generator.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X6qQzoAPrSRNzl3cQcMWasoPv3eK56sIlAOTeay61No/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gather an army of Rage! Random Garou Generator.</a><br /> Shapeshifting Historian<br /> Writer - Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Werewolf: the Forsaken, Exalted 3e, TC: \u00c6on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","name":"nikink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}